xhci: accept an event ring of several segments

The xHCI model cached one event ring segment and declared the host
controller dead (USBSTS.HCE) for any ERSTSZ but 1.  The spec allows a
segment table, and a Novatek vendor kernel (NA51090, NT98633: Linux
4.19.148's xhci with ERST_NUM_SEGS 4) asks for four: every event after
the first reset was dropped, so the kernel saw no command completion and
enumerated nothing.

Keep the segment table (up to XHCI_ERST_MAX, 8) and count the ring's
entries across it: the enqueue index, the dequeue pointer's index and
the full / EHB checks all run on that one index, mapped to and from
guest addresses through the table.  HCSPARAMS2 still advertises one
segment, so guests that follow it see no change.  post_load re-reads
the table from the guest's ERST.

diff --git a/hw/usb/hcd-xhci.c b/hw/usb/hcd-xhci.c
